Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:03:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/intel/oc_mailbox: Fix inverted plane status check

set_plane_undervolt() returns true on success, but the caller sets the
status bit for a plane when the call succeeds. As a result, a fully
successful run logs "plane programming failed, status = 0x3f" (0x1f
without the digital I/O plane) at error level, while a run where every
plane fails logs that all planes were programmed successfully.

Set the bit when programming a plane fails, so that the status reports
the failed planes as the log message says. Only the log output changes.

Fixes: commit fa68b6668623 ("drivers/intel/oc_mailbox: Add OC_MAILBOX undervolt driver")

TEST=Built for google/mccloud and lenovo/w541 with undervolting enabled.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/drivers/intel/oc_mailbox/oc_mailbox.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/intel/oc_mailbox/oc_mailbox.c b/src/drivers/intel/oc_mailbox/oc_mailbox.c
index f318e49b5..3cf5b449c 100644
--- a/src/drivers/intel/oc_mailbox/oc_mailbox.c
+++ b/src/drivers/intel/oc_mailbox/oc_mailbox.c
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@ static void oc_mailbox_undervolt(void)
 	 */
 	for (enum oc_mailbox_plane i = 0; i <= last_plane; i++) {
 		const unsigned int undervolt_mv = get_uint_option(plane_opt_names[i], 0);
-		if (set_plane_undervolt(i, undervolt_mv))
+		if (!set_plane_undervolt(i, undervolt_mv))
 			status |= 1 << i;
 	}
 	if (status == 0)
